External programs (not distributed with this software)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

videofx executes FFmpeg's `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` as separate programs, via the
operating system's process interface and their documented command-line
interfaces.  No FFmpeg source or object code is included in, linked into, or
distributed with videofx; the user supplies their own build.  FFmpeg is
licensed under the LGPL 2.1 or later, and, depending on how it was configured,
possibly the GPL 2 or later -- notably, builds configured with --enable-gpl
(as are required for libx264, libx265, and libvidstab) are GPL-licensed.
FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard, originator of the FFmpeg project.

The optional `warp-stabilizer` effect additionally requires an FFmpeg build
that includes libvidstab (vid.stab, Copyright (C) Georg Martius, licensed
under the GPL version 2 or later), and `videofx calibrate` requires one that
includes libvmaf (Netflix VMAF, licensed under the BSD+Patent license).  Both
are reached only as filters inside the user's own FFmpeg binary.

The FIT protocol and FIT file format are proprietary to Garmin and are subject
to Garmin's FIT Protocol License.  This project reads FIT files using an
independent third-party Go implementation (github.com/muktihari/fit) and
neither includes nor distributes any part of Garmin's FIT SDK.  This project
is not affiliated with or endorsed by Garmin.
